{"title":"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems#Problem_10\" title=\"2021 AMC 10B Problems\">2021 AMC 10B #10</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems#Problem_6\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems\">2021 AMC 12B #6</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(3D_Geometry_-_Cones_and_Cylinders)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (3D Geometry - Cones and Cylinders)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An inverted cone with base radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc7c6c1d0a2250475701d6a0d2df2c93a8e002fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12  \\mathrm{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e9a71f1276d7f86422c8c92b73865cf721f4a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18  \\mathrm{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> is full of water. The water is poured into a tall cylinder whose horizontal base has radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77b4b89a8c3384feb49876bb7e3e24ac4f867cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24  \\mathrm{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. What is the height in centimeters of the water in the cylinder?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5ffa6e2276ad2d5be15f35d385c0605cf1774e89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~1.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~3 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~4 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~4.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"377\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of a cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb8b00aba4e33fc15ce064c3363026ea9b33552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot\\pi \\cdot r^2 \\cdot h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the base radius and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the height. The water completely fills up the cone so the volume of the water is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54f0483974111f7a0935bd488a96afbefae8a249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot18\\cdot144\\pi = 6\\cdot144\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"180\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>The volume of a cylinder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/8/a88e3a9ac5584a93316b9d1a926682df733d8833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\cdot r^2 \\cdot h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" /> so the volume of the water in the cylinder would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/730563d7c99242f9e7bb9ca865d30b4314f62d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24\\cdot24\\cdot\\pi\\cdot h$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"97\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>We can equate these two expressions because the water volume stays the same like this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f8ae8bb7c14f8cd62274ea9926ea2effc82a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24\\cdot24\\cdot\\pi\\cdot h = 6\\cdot144\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"181\" height=\"13\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/692feec8d7e383a81e7c8a4ba8512b70a07767bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4h = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4ce1d9bf0f74086d98f733e78b4185bfd55f476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=\\frac{6}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d068281c9a66173f5fe9be713d5815ab7fa5f1ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~1.5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~abhinavg0627\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The water completely fills up the cone. For now, assume the radius of both cone and cylinder are the same. Then the cone has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the volume of the cylinder, and so the height is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then, from the problem statement, the radius is doubled, meaning the area of the base is quadrupled (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb0e6e64d73bacef9c8869039bc21581f1884e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />).\n</p><p>Therefore, the height is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de68058201dde4d911a6e48b0cb4dde2e5ec7f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 \\div 3 \\div 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~1.5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"181\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~PureSwag\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=qpvS2PVkI8A&amp;t=509s\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=qpvS2PVkI8A&amp;t=509s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.283D_Geometry_-_Cones_and_Cylinders.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(3D_Geometry_-_Cones_and_Cylinders)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (3D Geometry - Cones and Cylinders)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (3D Geometry - Cones and Cylinders)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4JhZLAORb8c\">https://youtu.be/4JhZLAORb8c</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Hawk Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VzwxbsuSQ80\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VzwxbsuSQ80</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GYpAm8v1h-U?t=1068\">https://youtu.be/GYpAm8v1h-U?t=1068</a> (for AMC 10B)\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kuZXQYHycdk\">https://youtu.be/kuZXQYHycdk</a> (for AMC 12B)\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DvpN56Ob6Zw?t=897\">https://youtu.be/DvpN56Ob6Zw?t=897</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Under_2_min.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Under 2 min!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6O32bUIvNEo\">https://youtu.be/6O32bUIvNEo</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B\">2021 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Pr